.TH REMPKG-FORMAT 5 "September 2026" "REM package format" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
rempkg-format \- REM local package archive layout
.SH DESCRIPTION
A version 1 REM package is a gzip-compressed tar archive. It contains one
JSON file named \fBrempkg.json\fR and a \fBpayload/\fR tree whose paths are
relative to the target filesystem root.
.PP
The JSON object contains \fBformat\fR (integer 1), \fBname\fR,
\fBversion\fR, \fBarch\fR, \fBdescription\fR and a \fBfiles\fR array.
Each array item records a relative \fBpath\fR, \fBtype\fR, permission
\fBmode\fR and, for regular files, a SHA-256 \fBsha256\fR digest. Symlink
entries record the relative \fBtarget\fR. Supported types are regular file,
directory and symlink. Device nodes and hard links are rejected.
.SH PATH RULES
Paths must be relative and cannot contain a parent-directory component.
Symlink targets must be relative and resolve lexically within the package
root. No payload path may descend through a symlink. Install refuses to
overwrite existing non-directory objects.
.SH SECURITY
The digest detects payload corruption but does not authenticate the publisher.
Only install archives from a trusted source. Version 1 has no signatures,
dependency metadata, hooks, upgrade protocol or crash-recovery journal.
.SH SEE ALSO
rempkg(1), REM_PACKAGE_SYSTEM.md
